(Title) Tj
T*
(A Community Venue-Based HIV Prevention Initiative Targeting Men: Protocol for Assessing) Tj
T*
(Feasibility, Acceptability, and Preliminary Effectiveness in a Sub-Saharan African Setting) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Men in high-transmission settings show low engagement with conventional HIV prevention) Tj
T*
(services. Non-traditional community venues may offer opportunities for outreach and) Tj
T*
(behavior change support. This protocol describes a cluster-randomized trial evaluating a) Tj
T*
(barbershop-based HIV prevention program in a high-transmission district in Uganda.) Tj
T*
(Approximately 250 men frequenting participating barbershops will be enrolled and followed) Tj
T*
(for 12 months. Barbershops will be randomly assigned to either the intervention program) Tj
T*
(\(including HIV education delivered by trained barbers, free self-testing kits, and peer-) Tj
T*
(support discussion groups\) or standard care. Primary outcomes include program feasibility) Tj
T*
(metrics \(reach, attendance, session fidelity\) and participant-reported acceptability.) Tj
T*
(Secondary outcomes include self-reported HIV testing completion, changes in sexual risk) Tj
T*
(behaviors, and interest in or use of biomedical prevention services. Exploratory outcomes) Tj
T*
(include incident sexually transmitted infections. Data will be collected through) Tj
T*
(participant surveys, clinical specimens, and implementation metrics at baseline, 6 months,) Tj
T*
(and 12 months.) Tj
